event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1050,"item_id":"fc_09e7677d2c9d8e14016adb2f7175688191ba9810b095ce7535","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"irreducibility of M tensor_Z K under L(K)\\\",\\\"obstacle_assessment\\\":{\\\"classification\\\":\\\"ROUTINE_COMPLETION_NOT_SUBSTANTIVE_GAP\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The J facts follow from matrix-unit decomposition and elementary finite-module calculations. No substantive defect exists.\\\"},\\\"complete_proof\\\":\\\"Let R=Z_(p), n=lambda+1, and e_i=y^i v/i! for 0<=i<=lambda in the characteristic-zero module. From the sl2 relations and highest-weight equations, iteration gives X_r e_i=binom(lambda-i+r,r)e_(i-r) and Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r), with out-of-range indices zero, where X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r!. Let E_ab be the matrix unit sending e_b to e_a. These formulas give Y_lambda X_lambda=E_lambda,lambda; X_(lambda-i)E_lambda,lambda=E_i,lambda; E_lambda,lambda Y_(lambda-j)=binom(lambda,j)E_lambda,j. Because lambda<p, binom(lambda,j) is a unit of R. Thus all E_i,j belong to the R-algebra generated by divided powers. Admissibility implies those operators preserve M_R=R tensor_Z M.\\n\\nSet J_i={c in C: c e_i is in M_R}. Since M_R is finite free over R, its image E_ii(M_R)=J_i e_i is finitely generated, so J_i is finitely generated. It is nonzero because M_R spans the complex module and E_ii is a nonzero projection. If c is in J_j, E_ij(c e_j)=c e_i is in M_R; reversing i,j proves all J_i equal J. For m in M_R, each E_ii m is in M_R, so each coordinate is in J e_i. Conversely the definition of J gives J e_i subset M_R. Hence M_R=direct_sum_i J e_i.\\n\\nLet Q be the fraction field of R. Tensor this decomposition with Q. Since M_R has rank n, n=n dim_Q(Q tensor_R J), so J has rank one. J is torsion-free as a submodule of C. Identify Q tensor_R J with Q; the image I of J is a nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of Q. Clearing denominators gives a nonzero finitely generated ideal dI of R. Every nonzero q in Q has form p^k u for integer k and unit u in R. For a finite set of nonzero generators of an ideal, choose the smallest such exponent k; all generators are in p^k R and one is p^k times a unit, so the ideal equals p^k R. Thus dI is principal and J is free of rank one. Choose a generator a. Then a e_i form an R-basis of M_R.\\n\\nOn this basis, x(ae_i)=(lambda-i+1)ae_(i-1), y(ae_i)=(i+1)ae_(i+1), and h(ae_i)=(lambda-2i)ae_i. Reducing modulo p gives the standard module on the reduced basis. Localization and reduction identify M_R/pM_R with M tensor_Z F_p: a Z-basis of M yields the same reduced basis and the same reduced integral action matrices. Extending scalars from F_p to K gives an L(K)-module isomorphism with the standard reduced module over K.\\n\\nIn that module, for r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of powers of x and y. The matrix-unit identities remain valid modulo p, since binom(lambda,j) is nonzero modulo p. Any subspace W invariant under x,y,h is consequently invariant under every E_i,j. Given a nonzero vector w=sum_i c_i e_i in W, select i with c_i nonzero. Then E_ji w=c_i e_j for every j, so all basis vectors belong to W and W is the whole module. The module has dimension lambda+1>0. This includes lambda=0; no step requires p>2 or distinct reduced h-weights.\\\",\\\"source_obligations\\\":\\\"No general literature theorem is imported. The divided-power formulas follow by iteration from the supplied sl2 relations and highest-weight equations. Matrix-unit identities and all R-module arguments are derived explicitly above. The characteristic-zero basis and dimension, the admissible lattice properties, and action setup are supplied by the frozen context and hypotheses.\\\",\\\"edge_cases\\\":\\\"lambda=0 gives the one-dimensional module and identity matrix unit. p=2 is included, with lambda=0 or 1 and no division by 2. M is arbitrary admissible, not restricted to a particular lattice. Any field K of characteristic p follows by scalar extension from F_p.\\\"}\"}"}

